# Android (TWA)
# The generated Gradle project is build output — `node scripts/build-twa.mjs`
# recreates it. twa-manifest.json is generated too, from the environment.
android-twa/
# Signing keys never go in a repository. Play ties an app to its key forever:
# a leaked key lets someone else ship an update to your users, and a lost one
# means republishing under a new listing.
*.keystore
*.jks


# The signing key password lives beside the key; neither belongs in git.
*.keystore.pass
*.pass.*.bak

# Scratch copies of host config, pasted in for debugging
temp/
my-publishing-studies/competition.md

# ── Kept on disk, kept out of the repo ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# Two ignored directories, each its own git repository, each with a reason:
#
#   server/       how THIS deployment is built — firewall, mail, backups. Not a
#                 secret exactly; a map, and one that only helps an attacker.
#   development/  how this is BEING built — the queue, the planning, the notes
#                 written straight to the agent. Nobody else's business.
#
# Both are still here and still used every day. They have their own history in
# their own private repos, because these files are worth versioning; they are
# just not worth publishing. A public repo ships its whole history.
#
# AGENTS.md and TODO.md at the root are symlinks into development/, so the
# things that expect them there still find them.
server/
development/
AGENTS.md
TODO.md
CLAUDE.md
